\begin{cases}
5(a + 2d) = 70 \\
10(a + 4.5d) = 210
\end{cases}
\]
Simplifying these equations, we get: \[
\begin{cases}
a + 2d = 14 \\
a + 4.5d = 21
\end{cases}
\]
Subtracting the first equation from the second, we get \(2.5d = 7\), so \(d = \frac{14}{5}\). Substituting \(d = \frac{14}{5}\) back into the first equation, we get \(a + 2 \left(\frac{14}{5}\right) = 14\), so \(a + \frac{28}{5} = 14\), and thus \(a = 14 - \frac{28}{5} = \frac{70}{5} - \frac{28}{5} = \frac{42}{5}\). \end{think} <answer> \frac{42}{5} \end{answer}

